.env
*.db
nexton.db
*.exe

# SQLite WAL sidecars.
#
# These are runtime state, not source: `-shm` is a process-scoped shared-memory
# index (SQLite rebuilds it on open) and `-wal` holds recent commits not yet
# checkpointed into the main file. They are rewritten on every run and are only
# meaningful alongside the exact `nexton.db` that produced them — which is not
# tracked either. `*.db` above does not match these suffixes, which is how they
# were first staged.
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Local Go build/test caches. Created when the toolchain's default cache
# location is not writable (a sandbox, for instance) and redirected here.
# Large and machine-specific, so never committed.
.gocache/
.gomodcache/
.gotmp/